  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-15T22:59:31.369Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You probably heard it more than enough that the \"upright\" value gets set to 1.00 whenever you either open the menu, get into a station/chair or disable it within the locomotion/action layer itself.\nWhile we can do certain actions to prevent the locomotion controller to transist upwards all the way, we can't to that for Desktop, since their standing upright value is 1.00 . \nWould it be possible, that you change the value upright gets set to to 1.01 ? We could do easy \"upright less 1.01\" checks and would erase that \"open your menu in desktop while proning folds your avatar\" issues as well as make sure no unwanted transitions in a desktop only tree would occur.\nFor 3p tracking we can say \"less 1.00\" since one does not instantaneous go up to with the headset. However, since for desktop 1.00 is the only indication if you are standing or not, we cant do that there.\nPossible suggestions:\n- have an additional boolean telling if the avatar is in a state where upright is supposed to be tracked\n- change upright's value to 1.01 (idk if its possible btw, its just an idea) whenever locomotion gets disabled or menu opened.",
